=============================================================================
Operating system base image and packages
=============================================================================

The container images are built on the ubuntu:22.04 base image. It contains
software distributed under a variety of free and open source licenses,
including the GNU General Public License. Canonical Ltd. publishes the
Ubuntu base images.

In addition, the following Ubuntu packages (and their dependencies) are
installed into the scala base image with apt-get, unmodified:

  software-properties-common, apt-utils   GPL-2.0
  curl                                    curl License (MIT/X derivative)
  wget                                    GPL-3.0-or-later
  gpg (GnuPG)                             GPL-3.0-or-later
  zip, unzip                              Info-ZIP License
  vim                                     Vim License
  telnet, inetutils-ping                  BSD-4-Clause-UC / GPL-3.0-or-later
  silversearcher-ag                       Apache-2.0 (see above)
  locales (GNU C Library)                 LGPL-2.1-or-later

The licenses of the individual packages are recorded in
/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright inside each image, and the corresponding
source is available from https://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/ (or
https://ports.ubuntu.com/ for arm64).

Ubuntu is a registered trademark of Canonical Ltd.
